    fullDescription: "The ArtScience Museum is one of the most striking buildings on the Marina Bay waterfront — a gleaming white structure shaped like an open lotus flower, designed by Moshe Safdie, the same architect behind the neighbouring Marina Bay Sands, and opened in 2011. Its ten 'petals' rise to skylights that funnel rainwater down through the building into a central pool, a poetic fusion of form and function that gives the museum its name. Inside, it stages ambitious touring blockbusters — past shows have covered everything from the Titanic and Leonardo da Vinci to marine biology and pop culture — but the star attraction is 'Future World: Where Art Meets Science', a permanent, ever-evolving collaboration with the Japanese collective teamLab. Across a series of darkened halls, digital projections respond to your movement and touch: waterfalls cascade over rocks, flowers bloom and scatter, shoals of light swim around you, and a mirrored 'Crystal Universe' surrounds visitors with drifting points of light. It is genuinely magical and one of Asia's best immersive art experiences, hugely popular with families and photographers alike. Tickets to Future World are S$21, with combined passes for the touring exhibitions. Visit on a weekday morning to enjoy the interactive rooms in relative calm, and pair it with a stroll around Marina Bay and the light show at nightfall.",
