    fullDescription: "Singapore Zoo is a world-class family destination, regularly ranked among the best zoos on the planet, and its pioneering open-concept design — where animals are separated from visitors by moats and vegetation rather than bars and cages — makes for an immersive, natural experience that thrills children and adults alike. Set in 26 hectares of lush rainforest in the Mandai wildlife precinct, it is home to more than 4,200 animals, and its layout is wonderfully geared to families: shaded walkways, plenty of rest spots, tram and boat rides to spare little legs, and animal feeding sessions and keeper talks throughout the day. The undoubted highlights for children are the free-ranging orangutans swinging through the canopy overhead, the elephant presentations, the playful otters and the walk-through Fragile Forest biodome. Best of all is Rainforest Kidzworld, a dedicated children's zone with a splash-and-play water park, pony and animal rides, a small farmyard and interactive play areas, so it is well worth packing swimwear and a towel for a mid-visit cool-down. For an unforgettable treat, the famous Jungle Breakfast lets families eat a buffet in the company of the orangutans (an extra fee applies and it must be booked ahead). Tickets are S$49 for adults and S$34 for children aged 3 to 12, with multi-park options covering the neighbouring River Wonders, Bird Paradise and Night Safari for better value. Allow the best part of a day, go early to catch the animals at their most active and to beat the heat, and bring hats, sunscreen and water. Educational, beautifully designed and endlessly engaging, it is a must for any family visiting Singapore.",
