    fullDescription: "River Wonders, formerly known as the River Safari, is the only river-themed wildlife park in the world and one of the most charming members of Singapore's Mandai wildlife family, sitting between the Singapore Zoo and the Night Safari. It takes visitors on a journey along recreations of the world's great rivers — the Mississippi, Congo, Nile, Ganges, Mekong and Yangtze among them — each populated by the fish, reptiles and animals of its region, displayed in a series of beautifully themed habitats and giant freshwater aquariums. The park's biggest stars are its giant pandas, Kai Kai and Jia Jia, lounging and munching bamboo in a climate-controlled enclosure that is a guaranteed hit with children, along with red pandas, manatees gliding through a vast Amazon flooded-forest tank, giant river otters, and one of the world's largest freshwater aquarium collections. Two boat rides add gentle adventure: the Amazon River Quest, a mild safari-style cruise past free-ranging animals such as jaguars and tapirs along the banks, and the Reservoir Cruise across the adjoining lake. The scale is more manageable than the main zoo, making it well suited to younger children and shorter attention spans, and it can be comfortably explored in around half a day. Tickets are S$42 for adults and S$30 for children aged 3 to 12, with multi-park passes covering the neighbouring attractions offering the best value if you plan to see more than one. Combine it with the Singapore Zoo for a full day in Mandai, or pair it with the Night Safari for a day-into-evening wildlife double bill. Engaging, educational and gentle, it is a lovely family outing.",
