    fullDescription: "Adventure Cove Waterpark on Sentosa is a fantastic family day out and the perfect way to cool off in Singapore's year-round heat, combining the thrills of a water park with the wonder of an aquarium. Its six water slides range from gentle family rides to the adrenaline-pumping Riptide Rocket, Southeast Asia's first hydro-magnetic coaster, which propels riders uphill as well as down, and the near-vertical Pipeline Plunge and Bluwater Bay wave pool for splashing about. But what really sets Adventure Cove apart is its marine element: the Adventure River, a lazy river that carries you on a rubber tube not just past waterfalls and grottoes but through a tunnel beneath a living reef, and, best of all, Rainbow Reef, where you can snorkel among more than 20,000 colourful tropical fish in a warm, safe lagoon, an experience that delights children and adults and requires no prior experience. There are also ray and shark encounters for the more adventurous. Facilities are excellent, with loungers, cabanas, changing rooms, lockers and food outlets, though loungers go quickly, so arrive at the 10:00 opening to claim a spot. Tickets are S$40 for adults and S$32 for children aged 4 to 12. Bring or buy reef-safe sunscreen, swimwear, towels and water shoes, and plan a full, relaxed day of splashing, sliding and snorkelling. Set within Resorts World Sentosa, it combines easily with the S.E.A. Aquarium next door or a beach afternoon, and for families with children who love the water it is one of the most enjoyable attractions in the whole city.",
