    fullDescription: "Gardens by the Bay is not just a feast for grown-up eyes but a wonderful place to bring children, combining free outdoor fun with jaw-dropping spectacle. The star for families is the Far East Organization Children's Garden, a dedicated and completely free zone with water-play areas where kids can run through fountains and splash pads to cool off (bring swimwear and a towel), along with adventure trails, rope bridges, a treehouse and a toddler play zone, all set among lush planting. Beyond it, the vast free outdoor gardens offer wide-open lawns for running around, sculptures and themed gardens to explore, and the extraordinary Supertree Grove, whose towering tree-like structures fascinate children by day and, at 19:45 and 20:45 each evening, come alive in the free Garden Rhapsody light-and-sound show, a genuinely magical experience for young and old that families spread out on the grass to watch. For a splurge, the two cooled conservatories add more wonder: the misty Cloud Forest with its 35-metre indoor waterfall, cave and treetop walkway, and the Flower Dome with its ever-changing displays, both a welcome air-conditioned break from the heat (combined ticket S$32; children under a certain height often reduced or free). The Floral Fantasy attraction and the OCBC Skyway aerial walkway add further options. With so much of it free, easy to reach by MRT and endlessly photogenic, Gardens by the Bay offers families a flexible day that can cost nothing or, with a few paid extras, fill many happy hours. Time your visit to end with the evening light show for a memorable finale.",
