    fullDescription: "The Night Safari offers families a genuinely different and memorable evening out, the world's first wildlife park designed to be experienced after dark, where more than 1,000 nocturnal animals roam softly lit habitats. For children old enough to stay up and appreciate it — generally around five and above — it is a thrilling adventure, full of the excitement of spotting creatures that a normal daytime zoo would never reveal, from prowling tigers and lions to elephants, rhinos, giraffes and the elusive smaller animals of the night. The easiest and most popular way to see it with kids is the 40-minute Wildlife Express tram, included in the ticket, which glides quietly through the geographically themed zones while a guide points out the animals, keeping tired little ones seated and safe while still delivering plenty of wildlife. Four short walking trails let more energetic families get closer to specific habitats on foot, and the entertaining Creatures of the Night live animal show, staged at 19:30 and 21:30, is a firm favourite that reveals the natural talents of various nocturnal species. The park opens at 19:15, so it works well as an evening activity after a restful afternoon, and there are restaurants on site for dinner before or during your visit. Tickets are S$56 for adults and S$39 for children aged 3 to 12, with multi-park passes for the Mandai attractions offering savings. Do note that very young children may find the darkness and the wait past bedtime challenging, and that flash photography is banned to protect the animals. For families with older kids, though, this atmospheric after-dark safari is one of the most distinctive experiences Singapore has to offer.",
