    fullDescription: "The Science Centre Singapore is one of the best rainy-day and beat-the-heat family attractions in the city, a huge, engaging science and technology museum in the western district of Jurong East that has been sparking children's curiosity for decades. Its great strength is that almost everything is hands-on: across a sprawling complex of galleries, more than a thousand interactive exhibits invite kids to push, pull, build, experiment and play their way through the principles of physics, biology, chemistry, mathematics and technology, from illusions and mirror mazes to electricity demonstrations, a walk-through of the human body, robotics, and ever-changing special exhibitions. Live science shows — including dramatic demonstrations involving fire, electricity and, at certain times, a spectacular Tesla-coil lightning display — add wow moments throughout the day, and the on-site Omni-Theatre offers immersive dome-screen films. The centre is designed for genuine learning through fun, and children can easily spend three or four absorbing hours here without noticing they are being educated. Adjacent to the main building sits Snow City, an indoor snow park with a sledding slope where kids can experience real snow and sub-zero temperatures — a novelty in tropical Singapore and a fun way to cool off, available as a separate ticket. Entry to the Science Centre is very affordable at around S$12 for adults and S$8 for children, with discounts for Singapore residents, making it one of the best-value family days out in the city. Fully indoor and air-conditioned, easily reached by MRT, and endlessly stimulating, it is the perfect choice for a hot afternoon, a wet day, or simply a break from the tourist trail with inquisitive children.",
