    fullDescription: "Changi Airport, routinely voted the best airport in the world, sets the tone for Singapore's superb transport from the moment you land, and getting into the city could hardly be easier. The cheapest option is the MRT: from the station beneath Terminals 2 and 3 (with Terminal 4 linked by shuttle), the green East–West Line runs to the centre, requiring a quick cross-platform change at Tanah Merah, for well under S$3 — unbeatable value, though the journey takes around 45 minutes to an hour and involves handling your luggage on the train, so it best suits daytime arrivals travelling light. For door-to-door comfort, the airport's famously orderly taxi ranks offer metered fares to downtown of roughly S$25 to S$40, with modest airport, late-night and peak surcharges, while ride-hailing via Grab works from designated pick-up points at similar prices; both take 20 to 30 minutes depending on traffic. There is also a convenient shared airport shuttle to city hotels for around S$10 per person, bookable at arrivals, and public buses for the truly budget-conscious. Whichever you choose, the airport is a joy to move through, with the stunning Jewel complex and its indoor waterfall attached should you have time to spare. To pay for the MRT and buses you can tap a contactless bank card or buy a stored-value or tourist transit pass. For departure, allow extra time not because the airport is slow — it is wonderfully efficient — but because you may want to enjoy Jewel and the terminals themselves. In short, Changi to the city is quick, cheap and painless by any method.",
