    fullDescription: "The Singapore Grand Prix is one of the jewels of the Formula 1 calendar and one of the biggest events of the city's year, a spectacular street race held each September on the Marina Bay Street Circuit. When it debuted in 2008 it made history as Formula 1's first-ever night race, and that remains its signature: the cars scream around a floodlit street circuit that winds past the illuminated landmarks of the bay — the Singapore Flyer, the colonial district, the Esplanade and the glittering skyline — under the tropical night sky, creating a uniquely glamorous and dramatic spectacle that looks stunning both trackside and on television. But the Singapore GP is far more than a motor race; it is a full-blown entertainment festival. Each evening of the three-day race weekend, ticket holders enjoy huge live concerts by major international music stars, who have over the years included some of the biggest names in the world, along with a carnival atmosphere of food, bars, roving performers and after-parties across the circuit's various zones. This combination of racing, music and nightlife draws a huge international crowd and gives the whole city a buzz. The trade-off is that it is a peak period: tickets, which range from more affordable walkabout passes to premium grandstand and hospitality packages, sell fast, and hotel prices, especially those near or overlooking the circuit, rise sharply and book out well in advance, so early planning is essential. Even for non-fans, the electric atmosphere, the concerts and the sheer spectacle of the floodlit night race make it a thrilling time to be in Singapore, and for motorsport lovers it is a bucket-list event.",
